You're welcome! Passing LLMs (or any shared resources) to LangGraph node functions can be done in several clean ways. Here's a production-focused approach using dependency injection and configuration:

1. Using a Shared Context Class (Recommended)

python
Copy
# app/core/context.py
from pydantic import BaseModel
from langchain_core.language_models import BaseLanguageModel

class AppContext(BaseModel):
    llm: BaseLanguageModel
    search_client: Any  # Your search service client
    database: Any       # Database connection
    config: dict        # Configuration
    
    class Config:
        arbitrary_types_allowed = True
2. Initialize Context in Main Workflow Setup

python
Copy
# app/core/workflow.py
from langgraph.graph import StateGraph
from app.config.settings import get_settings
from app.core.context import AppContext

def create_workflow():
    settings = get_settings()
    
    # Initialize shared resources
    context = AppContext(
        llm=ChatOpenAI(
            temperature=0.5,
            model="gpt-4-turbo",
            api_key=settings.openai_api_key
        ),
        search_client=SearchClient(settings.search_api_key),
        config=settings.model_dump()
    )
    
    # Initialize workflow with context
    workflow = StateGraph(ResearchState)
    
    workflow.add_node("research", research_node(context))
    workflow.add_node("write", write_node(context))
    
    # ... rest of workflow setup
    return workflow.compile()
3. Node Implementation with Context

python
